My translation:
let me watch awhile:
an ant's thoroughfare
and a cicada's shell

the Capatin also,
  came to bow to;
our Lord's spring

the perfumed 
robe, left unfolded;
spring dusk

on a bent nail 
a court-cap hangs;
a lodging in spring

spring evening
if there bird that’s not sleeping,
let it sing at the moon!

A sneeze —
then all is quiet;
summer mountain

A road of ants —
from a cloud peak,
continuing.

There are thorns;
Butterflies should be warned,
rose flowers.

I walk down a slope;
at the cold sunset glow
I shake my fist.

On the hill, a withered farm;
in the valley, no cogitation.
Clear water is all.

Of a lifetime,
the heart of now;
look at goldfish.

On the mirror, too,
the hand-print white;
talcum powder.

Talcum powder;
in the moonlight breeze,
it wore off.

Eel weir;
Kiso's night train
lights it and goes.

Rain seems imminent
as tango approaches;
father and son.

Goldfish bowl;
the Tenjin festival
begins to reflect.

A valley monk
being called by a peaks monk;
summer grove.
